Anyone here?

576
00:15:23,350 --> 00:15:24,220
Anyone here?

577
00:15:27,520 --> 00:15:28,480
(Wu Siying, Secure Love)
Wu Siying.

578
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:29,070
Hi, everyone.

579
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:30,040
The Yellow Space

580
00:15:30,040 --> 00:15:31,080
now has three girls.

581
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:32,280
I'm starting to worry

582
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:34,040
about the two guys in the Blue Space.

583
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:35,400
Are any girls going to show up for them?

584
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:36,280
Are they okay?

585
00:15:37,430 --> 00:15:38,150
We all picked

586
00:15:38,150 --> 00:15:38,770
the yellow card?

587
00:15:39,110 --> 00:15:39,690
Yeah.

588
00:15:40,070 --> 00:15:41,340
Were you torn when you chose?

589
00:15:41,340 --> 00:15:42,010
Yeah.

590
00:15:42,010 --> 00:15:42,700
Other than

591
00:15:42,700 --> 00:15:43,250
the green one,

592
00:15:43,250 --> 00:15:44,930
I debated all the others.

593
00:15:44,930 --> 00:15:45,800
There was a green one?

594
00:15:46,290 --> 00:15:46,730
Green

595
00:15:46,730 --> 00:15:47,560
is the one

596
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:48,390
about being independent.

597
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:49,280
Wow, is it really

598
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:49,920
that unpopular?

599
00:15:50,130 --> 00:15:50,930
Independent Love.

600
00:15:50,960 --> 00:15:51,260
Looks like

601
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:52,120
(No one's coming)
the Green Space is still empty.

602
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:52,720
Nobody's coming.

603
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:53,280
Send you over there.

604
00:15:53,340 --> 00:15:54,620
Send you.

605
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:55,680
(Someone will come)
Someone definitely will.

606
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:56,480
(I believe)
I believe it.

607
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:00,200
Which color did he pick?

608
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:03,540
(Green card)

609
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:04,040
Green card?

610
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:04,640
He picked the green one.

611
00:16:04,640 --> 00:16:05,160
Nice.

612
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:07,320
Here we go.

613
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:12,700
(Cao Yiheng, Independent Love)

614
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:14,300
(Not a freeze-frame)

615
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:15,520
Enjoying his independent space.

616
00:16:17,260 --> 00:16:18,180
(It gets darker and darker)

617
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:18,720
He waited until...

618
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:19,560
Wait until it got dark.

619
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:20,840
Now that's independent.

620
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:26,490
(Feeling bad for him)
This is kind of tragic.

621
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:27,780
I really want to ask if he regrets it.

622
00:16:27,780 --> 00:16:29,380
(Sits down again)

623
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:30,400
He's going stir-crazy.

624
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:31,560
I totally get it.

625
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,360
When I first entered

626
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:34,400
the house,

627
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:35,480
I was the first one in too.

628
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:37,480
Then everyone who came after me

629
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:38,400
went the wrong way

630
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:39,680
and ended up in other rooms.

631
00:16:39,680 --> 00:16:40,560
So I was alone,

632
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:41,560
wandering around the first floor,

633
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:42,480
then the second floor.

634
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:46,340
(Sun was just as "independent")

635
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:47,160
And then,

636
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:49,200
when someone finally showed up,

637
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:50,840
I felt like I'd been rescued.

638
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:53,400
That was brutal.

639
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:54,760
Let's see when he gets rescued.

640
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:00,480
Someone said hi.

641
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:02,400
(Hopeful)
Now he's really hopeful.

642
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:04,040
Really?

643
00:17:04,260 --> 00:17:04,600
(Walks past)

644
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:05,120
She walked right past.

645
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:06,480
She turned away.

646
00:17:06,480 --> 00:17:07,560
I feel for you.

647
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:11,040
Are all five girls already here?

648
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:11,800
Looks like it.

649
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:12,520
So, the Green Space

650
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:13,160
really only has...

651
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:14,480
Just him.

652
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:16,760
Wait, didn't Dinghao

653
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:17,920
pick the green card too?

654
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:19,760
(Same choice)
Dinghao, if you were there alone

655
00:17:19,760 --> 00:17:21,000
and had waited this long,

656
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:21,880
what would you be like?

657
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:24,240
I'd probably

658
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:25,240
start

659
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:26,600
to wonder if I picked

660
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:27,760
the wrong option.

661
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:29,440
But honestly,

662
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:31,600
when it comes to being

663
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:32,360
by myself,

664
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:33,680
I'm pretty okay with it.

665
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:34,800
I'd just

666
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:36,480
wonder why nobody else was coming

667
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:37,600
or choosing this one.

668
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:39,600
I'd probably find something to do.

669
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,840
If I knew for sure no one was coming,

670
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:44,320
I'd probably go visit the other rooms.

671
00:17:45,320 --> 00:17:46,360
That's pretty bold.

672
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:47,120
I mean,

673
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:48,240
it doesn't hurt to ask.

674
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:51,240
True.

675
00:17:51,740 --> 00:17:54,700
(Liang Renfang, Empathetic Love)

676
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:55,600
Finally, someone came.

677
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:58,280
Let's see if he says more
than a few words now.

678
00:17:59,090 --> 00:18:01,340
Hello.

679
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:03,360
What's wrong?

680
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:04,040
What happened?

681
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,250
Their reactions are both so cute.

682
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:06,100
I'll sit...

683
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:06,500
(Jumps)

684
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:07,480
Come, have a seat.

685
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:09,600
They both jumped up.

686
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:11,960
Neither of them knows what to do
with themselves.

687
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:13,580
You seem pretty outgoing.

688
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:14,970
I'm an ENFP.

689
00:18:15,540 --> 00:18:16,420
Then you must be super fun.

690
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:17,520
(Compliment)
ENFP?

691
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:18,520
She's the same as me.

692
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:20,640
A golden retriever energy.

693
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:23,540
Not bad.

694
00:18:24,320 --> 00:18:25,120
(Copying)
He's copying her.

695
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,400
I remember hearing something

696
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:28,320
about this in psychology.

697
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:30,080
I don't remember exactly,

698
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,680
but when you like someone...

699
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:33,280
You naturally copy
their movements, right?

700
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:35,370
I'm the little butterfly.

701
00:18:35,370 --> 00:18:36,200
Which one is that again?

702
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:37,480
Suddenly, he's talking a lot more.

703
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:38,520
No more one-word answers.

704
00:18:39,370 --> 00:18:40,530
I'm Yu Yang.

705
00:18:40,850 --> 00:18:42,780
My hobbies are...

706
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:44,230
walking.

707
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:45,780
(Cracks up)
Walking?

708
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:46,720
(And...)
Very healthy.

709
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:47,680
Traveling, I guess.

710
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:49,570
I drove the Duku Highway by myself.

711
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:51,320
That's so cool.

712
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:52,240
Very cool.

713
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:54,160
Wouldn't he be a better fit

714
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:54,640
for the Green Space?

715
00:18:55,580 --> 00:18:56,950
Very independent.

716
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:01,680
Do you guys prefer

717
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:02,480
taking trips like that on your own,

718
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:04,280
or do you always want friends with you?

719
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:07,280
I recently went to Xinjiang alone.

720
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:08,720
I joined a tour group,

721
00:19:08,720 --> 00:19:10,160
but after I left the group,

722
00:19:10,160 --> 00:19:12,200
I went to Kazakhstan by myself.

723
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:13,720
Did you go looking for Mi Die?

724
00:19:13,720 --> 00:19:14,440
No.

725
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:15,080
He wasn't there at the time.

726
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:15,880
I even asked him about it.

727
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:18,320
Honestly, traveling alone

728
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:19,720
is pretty great.

729
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:21,840
You wake up and decide
what you feel like doing,

730
00:19:21,840 --> 00:19:23,400
make a last-minute plan, and just go.

731
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,240
It feels really freeing.

732
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:26,200
Yeah.

733
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:28,680
I think they're just
two different modes.

734
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:30,920
After spending a lot of time
with friends,

735
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:32,280
you need some time alone

736
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:33,040
to recharge.

737
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:34,120
But if you're alone too long,

738
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:35,360
you start getting bored

739
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:36,640
and want to be around friends again.

740
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:38,280
Need some outside stimulation.

741
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:39,440
(Wants both)

742
00:19:39,440 --> 00:19:40,360
Then I'm a lot like you.

743
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:43,120
I'm totally fine going out on my own,

744
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:44,560
but if

745
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:45,640
my friends want to come with me,

746
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:46,560
I'm happy about that too.

747
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:50,200
I noticed

748
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:52,200
that once the girls arrived,
they started talking

749
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:53,680
about hobbies and interests.

750
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:56,320
Yifan, when you're talking
with just other girls,

751
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:58,000
is it different

752
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,240
from what you talk about
when guys are around?

753
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:00,140
(Is it different?)

754
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:00,960
I think so.

755
00:20:01,480 --> 00:20:03,280
Because you're curious
about different things.

756
00:20:03,520 --> 00:20:04,200
Really?

757
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:04,920
(How so?)

758
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:05,760
Like,

759
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:07,720
if it's all girls at first,

760
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:09,360
we might talk about things
like zodiac signs

761
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:10,960
or other stuff that we're interested in.

762
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:12,560
But when a guy suddenly joins,

763
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:14,120
the conversation naturally shifts

764
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:15,720
to what we're curious about with him.

765
00:20:16,660 --> 00:20:17,500
(Makes sense)

766
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:18,360
The guy's perspective.

767
00:20:18,380 --> 00:20:19,260
(Curious)

768
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:20,320
What about the guy's perspective?

769
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:21,160
(Curious +1)
Yeah, the guy's perspective.

770
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:23,140
(Thinking...)

771
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:24,880
Probably.

772
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:25,720
Yeah, I think it changes too.

773
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:29,240
Which space

774
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:30,960
stood out to you most?

775
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:31,880
For me,

776
00:20:31,880 --> 00:20:32,520
probably the yellow one.

777
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:33,040
I feel

778
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:34,040
that the girls in the Yellow Space

779
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:35,320
all have very unique personalities.

780
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:36,360
(The girls in the Yellow Space
all stand out)

781
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,560
You can immediately tell Cui Kaiyi

782
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:38,320
is very outgoing.

783
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:39,960
(Cui Kaiyi: Outgoing & warm)
She quickly broke the ice

784
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:42,200
with Sun Bohan and the others.

785
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:42,840
Sun Qimeng

786
00:20:42,840 --> 00:20:44,440
(Sun Qimeng: Gentle & attentive)
seems more observant.

787
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:45,040
And Wu Siying

788
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:45,880
(Wu Siying: Quiet & shy)
seems a little quieter.

789
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,160
The Yellow Space

790
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:49,560
stood out to me too.

791
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:50,680
First, there were a lot of people,

792
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:53,480
and the vibe stayed pretty comfortable.

793
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:57,320
You two are really observant.

794
00:20:57,840 --> 00:20:58,720
And

795
00:20:58,720 --> 00:21:00,560
it does feel like these choices

796
00:21:00,560 --> 00:21:01,280
actually reveal something different.

797
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:03,040
For example,

798
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:03,680
those in the Red Space

799
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:05,280
didn't turn out the way we expected.

800
00:21:05,280 --> 00:21:06,880
Everyone wasn't instantly
super outgoing.

801
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:08,680
Maybe that's because

802
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:09,680
this is the kind

803
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:10,880
of relationship

804
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:12,040
they hope to have.

805
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:14,920
Sometimes you choose exactly

806
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:16,120
what you feel you're missing.

807
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:17,240
For example,

808
00:21:17,240 --> 00:21:18,360
someone who's more passive might want

809
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:19,600
a partner who takes the lead.

810
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:21,120
And

811
00:21:21,120 --> 00:21:22,960
someone who's insecure

812
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:24,640
might want a partner

813
00:21:24,640 --> 00:21:26,240
who makes them feel safe.

814
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:27,400
As for the green one,

815
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:28,440
I think that one

816
00:21:28,440 --> 00:21:30,120
really requires boundaries
and independence.

817
00:21:30,120 --> 00:21:31,160
A very strong sense of self.

818
00:21:33,280 --> 00:21:34,480
This season's new cast

819
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:36,240
all seem
to have their own distinct traits.

820
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:37,160
It's pretty interesting.

821
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:38,400
Let's keep watching

822
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:40,200
and see if they all meet up.

823
00:21:44,980 --> 00:21:46,060
(The screen lights up)

824
00:21:46,260 --> 00:21:47,860
(They can see the other spaces)

825
00:21:48,800 --> 00:21:49,950
(Hi!)
It's like a video call.

826
00:21:49,950 --> 00:21:50,710
Can the others see us?

827
00:21:50,860 --> 00:21:52,170
So, we can see everyone from here?

828
00:21:52,760 --> 00:21:53,600
We had something like that too.

829
00:21:54,560 --> 00:21:56,000
We were split between two locations.

830
00:21:56,480 --> 00:21:57,680
One group was in Guangzhou,

831
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:58,880
while the other was in Shenzhen.

832
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:00,640
After we talked for a while,

833
00:22:00,640 --> 00:22:02,600
we met the other group on a live feed

834
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:03,920
before heading to the house.

835
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:05,800
We didn't have a giant screen like this

836
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:06,960
to see each other, though.

837
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:08,160
We even switched islands,

838
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:09,440
and you still couldn't meet everyone.

839
00:22:12,120 --> 00:22:12,860
A message came in.

840
00:22:16,340 --> 00:22:18,580
(Rule Message)
As a group,

841
00:22:18,580 --> 00:22:19,530
discuss and decide

842
00:22:19,530 --> 00:22:20,810
which Love Space to visit,

843
00:22:20,810 --> 00:22:21,690
then send the color

844
00:22:21,690 --> 00:22:23,090
you choose.

845
00:22:23,090 --> 00:22:24,860
So we have to move as a group?

846
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:25,840
They can switch spaces.

847
00:22:27,160 --> 00:22:28,760
So are the groups merging?

848
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:30,520
Like two spaces

849
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:31,740
(Which space gets first merge rights?)
meeting up together.

850
00:22:31,760 --> 00:22:32,400
Yeah, I think they're meeting.

851
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:33,080
Oh, merge rights.

852
00:22:33,890 --> 00:22:36,590
Hello.

853
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:37,580
They meet again.

854
00:22:37,580 --> 00:22:38,260
(Stares)

855
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:39,390
The first people they met.

856
00:22:39,440 --> 00:22:41,240
Red and blue always make a perfect pair.

857
00:22:42,610 --> 00:22:43,190
We...

858
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:44,430
Let's sit over here.

859
00:22:44,560 --> 00:22:45,010
Over here.

860
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:48,160
He looked twice.

861
00:22:49,360 --> 00:22:50,720
Is he waiting for the girl to sit first,

862
00:22:50,720 --> 00:22:51,240
then...

863
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:52,080
(Slowly moves closer)
See where she sits?

864
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:52,680
Yeah.

865
00:22:52,680 --> 00:22:53,440
He's moving closer.

866
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:54,080
So natural.

867
00:22:55,610 --> 00:22:56,300
Why do you want

868
00:22:56,300 --> 00:22:56,810
to choose

869
00:22:56,810 --> 00:22:57,520
the Red Space?

870
00:22:58,050 --> 00:22:58,260
Right.

871
00:22:58,260 --> 00:22:59,640
Personally...

872
00:22:59,640 --> 00:23:00,320
For me,

873
00:23:00,320 --> 00:23:01,530
I'd actually like to meet everyone.

874
00:23:02,170 --> 00:23:02,520
Yeah.

875
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:03,930
We met before. Don't you remember?

876
00:23:05,370 --> 00:23:06,130
Right.

877
00:23:06,130 --> 00:23:06,680
What I mean is...

878
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:07,410
Yeah.

879
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:09,400
He remembers, right?

880
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:10,120
He remembers.

881
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:10,760
I think he was just

882
00:23:10,760 --> 00:23:12,280
too shy to say it directly.

883
00:23:14,680 --> 00:23:16,240
We also talked a little

884
00:23:16,730 --> 00:23:17,540
about our food preferences.

885
00:23:17,540 --> 00:23:18,430
We wanted to hear yours too.

886
00:23:19,720 --> 00:23:20,760
I can't handle spicy food.

887
00:23:20,960 --> 00:23:21,880
She can't eat spicy food.

888
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:22,620
What? Aren't you from Chongqing?

889
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:23,560
Oh, she's from Chongqing.

890
00:23:24,050 --> 00:23:24,880
What about tofu pudding?

891
00:23:25,090 --> 00:23:26,790
Sweet or savory?

892
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:27,760
(Savory)
I always go sweet.

893
00:23:27,760 --> 00:23:28,840
I go savory.

894
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:29,960
If they have both sweet and savory,

895
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:30,880
I'd order both.

896
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:31,960
(Fair enough)
Okay.

897
00:23:32,930 --> 00:23:33,490
Hello.

898
00:23:34,520 --> 00:23:35,660
The independent guy is here.

899
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:36,960
(The lonely guy)
The independent guy is here.

900
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:38,930
Hello.

901
00:23:39,370 --> 00:23:40,410
Did you come from far away?

902
00:23:40,410 --> 00:23:41,450
Maybe a hundred yards.

903
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:42,520
No.

904
00:23:42,520 --> 00:23:44,590
I mean, where did you come from?

905
00:23:44,590 --> 00:23:45,390
From the entrance.

906
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:47,470
No, I mean which city?

907
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:52,100
From where you live

908
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:53,750
(or work)
He's accidentally hilarious.

909
00:23:53,750 --> 00:23:54,250
to get here.

910
00:23:54,250 --> 00:23:54,810
Oh, that's not far.

911
00:23:54,810 --> 00:23:56,280
Have you already forgotten

912
00:23:56,280 --> 00:23:57,590
our names?

913
00:23:57,700 --> 00:23:58,220
(Pop quiz)

914
00:23:58,610 --> 00:23:59,570
It's okay.

915
00:23:59,570 --> 00:24:00,210
We have plenty of time.

916
00:24:00,210 --> 00:24:01,140
There's a lot of time ahead.

917
00:24:01,700 --> 00:24:03,290
He used that to brush it off.

918
00:24:03,320 --> 00:24:04,330
(Did you catch that?)
He's telling himself it's okay.

919
00:24:04,330 --> 00:24:05,040
He moved right past it.

920
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:07,400
Smooth recovery.

921
00:24:07,400 --> 00:24:08,480
Very smooth recovery.

922
00:24:12,880 --> 00:24:13,680
What's this?

923
00:24:13,680 --> 00:24:14,960
Are those for voting?

924
00:24:15,510 --> 00:24:17,560
Write their name

925
00:24:17,560 --> 00:24:18,720
on the clear heart-shaped card.

926
00:24:18,960 --> 00:24:20,220
You can write up to three names.

927
00:24:20,240 --> 00:24:21,760
So each person can pick three?

928
00:24:22,320 --> 00:24:23,120
Yeah.

929
00:24:23,680 --> 00:24:25,320
(Who made the best first impression?)
Let's make our guesses.

930
00:24:25,320 --> 00:24:26,280
Which guy and girl

931
00:24:26,280 --> 00:24:28,640
got the most first-impression votes?

932
00:24:28,760 --> 00:24:29,600
Anyone who guesses right

933
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:31,040
gets a cute pillow.

934
00:24:32,920 --> 00:24:36,040
For the girls, I think it's probably...

935
00:24:36,760 --> 00:24:37,440
Cui Kaiyi.

936
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:38,800
Not really.

937
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:41,480
I think

938
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:43,800
people pick someone
who stood out right away.

939
00:24:44,600 --> 00:24:46,240
But Cui Kaiyi only met

940
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:47,200
two guys total.

941
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:48,920
Even if both vote for her,
that's only two votes.

942
00:24:50,520 --> 00:24:52,640
Over with Sha Yue'er,

943
00:24:52,640 --> 00:24:53,400
there are a lot more guys.

944
00:24:55,440 --> 00:24:55,800
Right.

945
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:56,440
Good point.

946
00:24:57,120 --> 00:24:58,040
So maybe the guys

947
00:24:58,040 --> 00:24:59,200
in the Yellow Space

948
00:24:59,200 --> 00:25:00,000
will get more votes.

949
00:25:00,240 --> 00:25:00,680
Yeah.

950
00:25:00,680 --> 00:25:01,600
But the girls

951
00:25:01,600 --> 00:25:02,760
in the Red Space may get more votes.

952
00:25:02,760 --> 00:25:03,880
For the girls, I think I'd...

953
00:25:03,880 --> 00:25:05,480
I'd probably pick Sha Yue'er.

954
00:25:05,500 --> 00:25:06,760
(Yifan's top pick:)
For the guy...

955
00:25:06,760 --> 00:25:07,560
(Girl: Sha Yue'er)

956
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:08,440
I'll make a dark-horse pick.

957
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:09,440
I'm going with Cao Yiheng.

958
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:10,140
(Guy: Cao Yiheng)

959
00:25:10,280 --> 00:25:11,360
Oh no, I want to copy your answer.

960
00:25:11,360 --> 00:25:12,360
Don't copy me.

961
00:25:14,480 --> 00:25:14,960
But I'm picking

962
00:25:14,960 --> 00:25:15,720
Cui Kaiyi.

963
00:25:16,320 --> 00:25:18,200
(Dinghao's top pick:)
In every conversation,

964
00:25:18,200 --> 00:25:20,080
(Girl: Cui Kaiyi)
she's one of the livelier people.

965
00:25:20,080 --> 00:25:21,520
Yeah, I think she's the type

966
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:22,920
who leaves a good impression easily.

967
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:25,600
For the guy, I'll pick...

968
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:31,760
Chen Hewen.

969
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:32,820
(Guy: Chen Hewen)

970
00:25:33,120 --> 00:25:34,800
I have another theory too.

971
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:36,320
(What's your theory?)

972
00:25:36,320 --> 00:25:38,920
On our season, people on the two islands

973
00:25:38,920 --> 00:25:40,280
had to choose one person to switch over,

974
00:25:40,280 --> 00:25:41,520
and we only had photos to go by.

975
00:25:42,360 --> 00:25:43,320
There were two guys.

976
00:25:43,320 --> 00:25:44,880
One wasn't smiling.

977
00:25:44,880 --> 00:25:46,200
Just posing with his lips closed.

978
00:25:46,200 --> 00:25:48,040
The other was smiling
with his teeth showing.

979
00:25:48,040 --> 00:25:49,320
The reason we chose who we did

980
00:25:49,320 --> 00:25:50,920
was basically the photo.

981
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:51,840
That bright energy.

982
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:53,120
Bright energy.

983
00:25:53,120 --> 00:25:54,400
(That makes sense)

984
00:25:54,400 --> 00:25:55,880
We thought he looked really cheerful,

985
00:25:55,880 --> 00:25:57,520
so we picked the one smiling
with his teeth.

986
00:25:58,120 --> 00:25:59,200
Then I'll choose

987
00:25:59,200 --> 00:26:01,000
Sun Bohan and Cui Kaiyi.

988
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,120
They had the biggest smiles.

989
00:26:02,180 --> 00:26:03,110
(Jingjun's top pick:)

990
00:26:03,120 --> 00:26:04,100
(Girl: Cui Kaiyi, Guy: Sun Bohan)

991
00:26:04,240 --> 00:26:05,400
What feels different

992
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:07,160
about this season's new cast?

993
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:09,120
They all seem pretty outgoing.

994
00:26:09,560 --> 00:26:10,200
Yeah.

995
00:26:10,200 --> 00:26:11,160
They seem easy to talk to.

996
00:26:11,160 --> 00:26:11,800
Very chatty.

997
00:26:12,800 --> 00:26:15,080
Cui Kaiyi stood out to me most.

998
00:26:15,080 --> 00:26:16,960
I'm not naturally

999
00:26:16,960 --> 00:26:18,480
that outgoing in social situations,

1000
00:26:18,480 --> 00:26:20,080
so I need someone

1001
00:26:20,080 --> 00:26:22,400
more outgoing

1002
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:23,640
to keep the energy up.

1003
00:26:23,640 --> 00:26:24,240
Right.

1004
00:26:24,800 --> 00:26:26,520
The person who stood out to me most

1005
00:26:26,520 --> 00:26:27,440
was probably Cui Yihang.

1006
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:30,040
Cui Yihang has this
really dry sense of humor.

1007
00:26:30,760 --> 00:26:31,240
Yeah.

1008
00:26:31,240 --> 00:26:32,640
And you can tell he's very thoughtful.

1009
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:34,480
He's constantly observing
what's going on.

1010
00:26:38,040 --> 00:26:42,280
Chen Hewen stood out to me most.

1011
00:26:43,040 --> 00:26:45,200
He carries himself really well.

1012
00:26:45,200 --> 00:26:47,960
He's polite and considerate
of everyone around him.

1013
00:26:47,960 --> 00:26:48,920
Yeah.

1014
00:26:48,920 --> 00:26:49,880
But I think

1015
00:26:49,880 --> 00:26:51,720
maybe because their choices
were so direct.

1016
00:26:52,040 --> 00:26:53,320
When you pick a certain space,

1017
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:54,120
you're more likely to meet people

1018
00:26:54,120 --> 00:26:56,560
who share similar views.

1019
00:26:56,560 --> 00:26:57,960
So it's easier to click quickly.

1020
00:26:57,960 --> 00:26:58,360
Exactly.

1021
00:26:58,360 --> 00:26:58,960
Could be.

1022
00:26:58,960 --> 00:27:01,640
You can really feel that all four colors

1023
00:27:01,640 --> 00:27:03,600
have their own distinct personalities,

1024
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:06,000
and the chemistry is different
when they come together.

1025
00:27:06,960 --> 00:27:08,000
(Can't wait)
I can't wait.

1026
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:09,000
I'm excited for the next episode.

1027
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:10,480
Let's take a group photo.

1028
00:27:10,480 --> 00:27:11,120
Okay.

1029
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:13,480
Watching Heart Signal with You,

1030
00:27:13,480 --> 00:27:14,880
the sparks never end.

1031
00:27:14,880 --> 00:27:16,360
See you next time.

1032
